## Frequently asked questions

### Do I need a computer science degree to get a developer job?

No. Many companies hire self-taught developers and bootcamp graduates. Some large companies and certain countries' visa rules still prefer degrees, so check each role.

### How many projects do I need in my portfolio?

Two or three strong, deployed projects are usually enough. Quality and your ability to explain them matter more than quantity.

### How many applications does it take to get a first developer job?

It varies widely. Many juniors apply to dozens or more roles. Tailored applications and referrals convert much better than mass applying.

### Should I take an unpaid internship?

Paid internships are better and more common in tech. If you consider an unpaid one, make sure you'll do real engineering work with mentorship, and check that it's legal where you live.

### Is QA or support a good path into development?

It can be. Many developers started in QA, support or data roles and moved internally. Choose a company that supports internal moves.

